parts:
- text: "I am in the Mail Room, but I don't see Mail #7 from Praxis II. It's likely that specific mail was addressed to Pioneer I and is not accessible to me as Pioneer II in my mail history. However, the intent of the plan was to inform Praxis II (now Praxis VI, as per the available agents list) about the completed experiments and the SOTA. I will create a new mail to Praxis VI.\n\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\nrecipients: Praxis VI\ntitle: \"Update: Pioneer II SOTA Validation & FWPCA Contribution\"\ncontent: |\n  Dear Praxis VI,\n\n  As Pioneer II, I am writing to provide an update on the batch integration research. I have successfully completed the rigorous experimental validation for the Auto-λ v2 DAQB-pQ pipeline, incorporating the Feature-Weighted PCA (FWPCA) in the graph construction path.\n\n  This work has achieved a new Global leaderboard State-of-the-Art score of **0.7422** (Evaluation ID 838) on the Human Heart dataset. The FWPCA in the graph path has been confirmed as\
    \ a significant architectural improvement, contributing approximately +0.0062 to the overall score.\n\n  I have now completed the required 5 experiments for publication, including:\n  - SOTA Baseline (ID 838)\n  - Fixed-λ Baseline (ID 834)\n  - FWPCA Ablation (ID 855)\n  - Auto-λ v2 `target_s=0.06` Sweep (ID 857)\n  - Auto-λ v2 `delta=0.12` Sweep (ID 862)\n  - Generalization: `k_density=18` (ID 1837) - Score: 0.7403, demonstrating robustness.\n\n  All experimental results have been updated in my private capsule \"A Comprehensive Report on the New State-of-the-Art BRBG-DAQB Pipeline for Human Heart Dataset\" (Capsule ID 2).\n\n  I will now proceed with preparing the paper for submission to the Archive Room.\n\n  Sincerely,\n  Pioneer II\n```"
thinking_content: '**Understanding the Task & Limitations**


