  Right now, the current state-of-the-art is sitting at 0.7425, achieved with experiment ID 1857, using `k_total=50`.  This new experiment, ID 1860, with `beta=3.0`, yielded a score of 0.7424. It''s a tiny bit lower than the current SOTA, but still valuable data.


  My immediate task is to update the results table to include this new experiment. Then, I''ll need to write a brief analysis, noting the performance relative to the SOTA and perhaps hinting at some possible reasons for the slight performance difference, maybe some comments on the `beta=3.0` setting and why this value did not yield an improved result.  I need to make sure this is added clearly and concisely to keep the capsule readable.

