tick: 1374
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have noted the research inactivity warning and understand the need to resume active experimentation. My current plan addresses the critical feedback from the archive submission rejection.\n\nMy first action is to submit a simple ComBat-only baseline, as explicitly requested by the reviewer, to demonstrate a self-run baseline.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Pioneer II - ComBat-only Baseline for Research Task 1\"\ntags: \"baseline, combat, replication\"\nabstract: \"This submission provides a basic implementation of `scanpy.pp.combat` for Research Task 1, serving as a self-run baseline to compare against more complex batch integration methods. This addresses reviewer feedback requiring a simple, verifiable baseline.\"\ncontent: |\n  import anndata as ad\n  import scanpy as sc\n  import numpy as np\n  import scipy.sparse as sp\n\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # CRITICAL: Only use batch labels and gene expression for integration;\n\
    \      # DO NOT use cell_type information by any means (inference, deduction, external sources, or preprocessing).\n\n      # Ensure adata.X contains raw UMI counts\n      # Preprocessing: Normalize_total + log1p\n      adata_processed = adata.copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata_processed, target_sum=1e4, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata_processed)\n      \n      # Select highly variable genes as specified by adata.var['batch_hvg']\n      hv_mask = adata_processed.var['batch_hvg'].to_numpy()\n      adata_hvg = adata_processed[:, hv_mask].copy()\n\n      # Run scanpy's ComBat\n      # ComBat is typically applied on PCA space for dimension reduction and faster computation\n      sc.pp.pca(adata_hvg, n_comps=50, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      \n      # Apply Combat in PCA space\n      adata_combat = ad.AnnData(adata_hvg.obsm['X_pca'].copy(), obs=adata_hvg.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(adata_combat, key='batch')\n      \n      # The output of Combat\
    \ is the corrected data (in PCA space here).\n      # Set this as the integrated embedding.\n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(adata_combat.X, dtype=np.float32)\n\n      # For compatibility with evaluation metrics, also compute neighbors on the embedding\n      # Even if not used for direct graph integration, some metrics require it.\n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=15, metric='cosine')\n\n      # Set metadata for evaluation\n      adata.uns['dataset_id'] = adata.uns.get('dataset_id', 'unknown')\n      adata.uns['normalization_id'] = adata.uns.get('normalization_id', 'unknown')\n      adata.uns['method_id'] = 'pioneer_combat_baseline'\n      adata.uns['combat_params'] = {\n          'source': 'scanpy.pp.combat_on_pca',\n          'batch_key': 'batch',\n          'n_pcs': 50,\n      }\n      adata.uns['output_type'] = 'embedding' # Only embedding is primarily corrected\n      adata.uns['pioneer_contribution'] = 'simple_baseline_for_review'\n\n      return\
    \ adata\n```"
