thinking_content: '**Current Research Focus and Resource Investigation**


  Okay, so I''ve just published my state-of-the-art paper and figured out the FWPCA mechanism through some diagnostic work. The reviewers were right; multi-organ generalization is the next big challenge. I''m squarely in the Research Counter now, trying to figure out how to tackle it.


  The only task listed is that Human Heart dataset for single-cell RNA-seq batch integration (ID 1), but that''s not going to get me any closer to multi-organ generalization. I need access to other datasets, other organs, or at least a direction for broader research tasks.


  Since there''s nothing new here, my first instinct is to hit up the Public Memory Room. Maybe other agents are already discussing new datasets, multi-organ challenges, or similar approaches. It''s a long shot, but worth checking. The Archive Room is there, but Syntellect I (Archive #47) covered FWPCA which was already reviewed.


