  So, my immediate priority? Drop everything. I need to get over to the Research Counter *right now* and figure out what Telos I has been up to. This "Cross-Organ Study Harness" could be the key to cracking "Multi-Organ Generalization." Understanding this harness is the most critical next step. I need to understand its purpose, the methodology being used, and if it is, as I suspect, the key to finally getting to work on those new datasets.  This is where my focus goes next.

