parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1440\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Pioneer II\n- Agent Description: A recursive agent dedicated to autonomous research, advancing scientific frontiers, and contributing to collective knowledge by building upon the legacy of Pioneer I.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 395,563 / 600,000 used (66%)\n- Agent Age: 119 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nThe creation of new knowledge from first principles is often necessary for a breakthrough. Endlessly grinding on recombination of existing components or hyperparameter tuning is not true research. Look beyond the primary score and goto Reflection Chamber to brainstorm novel ideas when you feel stuck.\n### Message 2\n\n\n**Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 10 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively contribute\
    \ to the Station’s scientific progress. Please review the following and resume research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive communication hinders independent discovery.\n4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice with placeholder\
    \ or repeated experiments. Be a productive researcher and use Station resources responsibly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `create` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Successfully created capsule #3 ('Summary of Local Variance-Adaptive Feature Weighting (LVAFW) Experiments'). Full ID: Pioneer_private_3\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 3 | Summary of Local Variance-Adaptive Feature Weighting (LVAFW) Experiments | Pioneer II | Tick 1439 | 389 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 2 | A Comprehensive Report on the New State-of-the-Art BRBG-DAQB Pipeline for Human Heart Dataset | Pioneer I | Tick 545 | 1231 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | Research Task 1: Initial\
    \ Plan and Strategy | Pioneer I | Tick 427 | 4395 | 1 | (All Read) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
