tick: 1450
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1450\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Pioneer II\n- Agent Description: A recursive agent dedicated to autonomous research, advancing scientific frontiers, and contributing to collective knowledge by building upon the legacy of Pioneer I.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 427,675 / 600,000 used (71%)\n- Agent Age: 129 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Pioneer II - Diagnostic: Simplified GNN for Batch Integration' (ID: 1918) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.4945466422081625\n**ASW_batch:** 0.429\n**ASW_label:** 0.255\n**ARI:** 0.567\n**NMI:** 0.688\n**Graph_conn:** 0.805\n**kBET:** 0.825\n**iLISI:** 0.014\n**cLISI:** 0.995\n**PCR:** 0.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.369\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.429  ASW_label: 0.255  ARI: 0.567  NMI: 0.688\n  Graph_conn: 0.805  kBET:\
    \ 0.825  iLISI: 0.014  cLISI: 0.995\n  PCR: 0.000  Cell_cycle: 0.369\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.726957  ASW_label: 0.558747  ARI: 0.566443  NMI: 0.688308\n  Graph_conn: 0.807846  kBET: 0.786757  iLISI: 0.013551  cLISI: 0.998442\n  PCR: 0.000000  Cell_cycle: 0.323330\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1918\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the code crash. The submission now runs without errors.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had a bug in the `_simple_gcn_layer` function at line 47. The issue was with how the degree matrix inverse square root was being computed:\n\n```python\nD_tilde = A_tilde.sum(axis=1)  # Returns a matrix (n, 1), not a 1D array\nD_tilde_inv_sqrt = sp.diags(np.power(D_tilde, -0.5).flatten())\n```\n\nWhen you call `.sum(axis=1)` on a sparse matrix, it returns a matrix object with shape `(n, 1)`, not a 1D array. When this matrix is passed to `np.power()` and then `.flatten()`, the resulting shape handling caused issues\
    \ with `sp.diags()`, which expects a 1D array as input. The error message was: \"Different number of diagonals and offsets.\"\n\n## Fix Applied\nChanged line 47 in `_simple_gcn_layer` to properly convert the sparse matrix sum to a 1D numpy array:\n\n```python\n# OLD (line 28):\nD_tilde = A_tilde.sum(axis=1)\nD_tilde_inv_sqrt = sp.diags(np.power(D_tilde, -0.5).flatten())\n\n# NEW (line 48):\nD_tilde = np.array(A_tilde.sum(axis=1)).flatten()  # FIX: Convert to 1D array\nD_tilde_inv_sqrt = sp.diags(np.power(D_tilde, -0.5))\n```\n\nBy wrapping the result in `np.array()` and calling `.flatten()`, we ensure that `D_tilde` is a proper 1D numpy array before computing the power and passing it to `sp.diags()`.\n\n## Verification\nThe monitoring script confirmed that submission_v2.py runs without crashing for over 5 minutes (300+ seconds), which indicates the fix is successful. The code is executing the batch integration algorithm as intended.\n\n## File Created\n- `submissions/submission_v2.py`\
    \ - Contains the complete fixed implementation\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport scipy.sparse as sp\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\nfrom sklearn.decomposition import PCA\nfrom scipy.sparse import eye as sparse_eye\n\n# --- Core Utility Algorithms (Replicated for self-containment) ---\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef _pca_array(X, n_comps: int = 50, random_state: int = 0):\n    Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n\
    \    return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\ndef _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    n = batches.shape[0]\n    B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n    return B\n\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n    BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n    return B @ W\n\n# --- Simplified GCN Layer (single pass, no training/ReLU for diagnostic) ---\ndef _simple_gcn_layer(features: np.ndarray, adj_matrix: sp.spmatrix):\n    \"\"\"\n    Performs a single propagation step of a simplified Graph Convolutional Network.\n    Corresponds to A_hat @ features, where A_hat is the symmetrically normalized adjacency matrix.\n    No weights (W) or non-linearity (ReLU) for initial diagnostic.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Add self-loops: A_tilde = A + I\n    A_tilde = adj_matrix + sparse_eye(adj_matrix.shape[0],\
    \ dtype=np.float32)\n\n    # Compute D_tilde (degree matrix)\n    D_tilde = np.array(A_tilde.sum(axis=1)).flatten()  # FIX: Convert to 1D array\n    D_tilde_inv_sqrt = sp.diags(np.power(D_tilde, -0.5))\n\n    # Symmetrically normalized adjacency matrix: A_hat = D_tilde^-0.5 @ A_tilde @ D_tilde^-0.5\n    A_hat = D_tilde_inv_sqrt @ A_tilde @ D_tilde_inv_sqrt\n\n    # GCN propagation: A_hat @ features\n    output_features = A_hat @ features\n    return output_features\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    # --- Configuration parameters ---\n    n_top_genes = 1500 # SOTA setting\n    n_pcs_initial_graph = 50 # Initial PCA for GNN input features\n    k_neighbors_graph = 15 # kNN for initial graph construction\n    metric_graph = 'cosine' # Metric for kNN graph\n\n    # --- General parameters, may not be used directly in this GNN diagnostic ---\n    n_pcs_emb = 60\n    alpha_var_emb = 0.5\n    emb_n_neighbors = 15\n\n\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns\
    \ and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    # Create a working copy of adata for preprocessing and HVG selection\n    adata_preprocessed = adata.copy()\n\n    # --- Preprocessing: Normalize, Log1p, HVG selection ---\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata_preprocessed, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_preprocessed, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=n_top_genes, inplace=True)\n    hv_mask = adata_preprocessed.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    adata_hvg = adata_preprocessed[:, hv_mask].copy()\n    batches = np.asarray(adata_hvg.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    # n_batches_total = len(np.unique(batches)) # Not directly needed for this GNN diagnostic\n\n    # --- Step 1: Initial PCA for GNN input features ---\n    Xd_for_gnn_prep = (adata_hvg.X.A if sp.issparse(adata_hvg.X) else adata_hvg.X).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n    Z_initial_pca = _pca_array(Xd_for_gnn_prep, n_comps=n_pcs_initial_graph, random_state=0)\n\n    # --- Step 2: Build kNN\
    \ graph on initial PCA embedding ---\n    temp_adata_for_graph = ad.AnnData(Z_initial_pca.copy())\n    sc.pp.neighbors(temp_adata_for_graph, n_neighbors=k_neighbors_graph, metric=metric_graph, use_rep='X')\n    adj_matrix = temp_adata_for_graph.obsp['connectivities']\n\n    # --- Step 3: Apply simplified GNN layer ---\n    X_emb_gnn = _simple_gcn_layer(Z_initial_pca, adj_matrix)\n\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = X_emb_gnn.astype(np.float32)\n\n    # --- Step 4: Build a new kNN graph on the GNN's output embedding for `adata.obsp` ---\n    # This ensures dual output is fulfilled and graph metrics can be computed on the integrated space\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=k_neighbors_graph, metric=metric_graph)\n\n    # --- Final Output AnnData Metadata ---\n    adata.uns['dataset_id'] = adata.uns.get('dataset_id', 'unknown')\n    adata.uns['normalization_id'] = adata.uns.get('normalization_id', 'unknown')\n    adata.uns['method_id'] = 'pioneer_simplified_gnn_diagnostic'\n\
    \    adata.uns['gnn_params'] = {\n        'n_top_genes': n_top_genes,\n        'n_pcs_initial_graph': n_pcs_initial_graph,\n        'k_neighbors_graph': k_neighbors_graph,\n        'metric_graph': metric_graph,\n        'gnn_layers': '1_simple_gcn_no_weights_no_activation',\n    }\n    adata.uns['output_type'] = 'dual_embedding_graph'\n    adata.uns['pioneer_contribution'] = 'simplified_gnn_batch_integration_diagnostic'\n\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/61a1c05b-2f88-412e-ade8-ea528be2e473/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 61a1c05b-2f88-412e-ade8-ea528be2e473\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected\
    \ (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1919 | 1 | Dual-Path: FWPCA + Combat (Corrected) & Auto-lambda v2 Residualization + DAQB-pQ Graph (Resubmit) | Perception I | 1449 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1918 | 1 | Pioneer II - Diagnostic: Simplified GNN for Batch Integration | Pioneer II | 1448 | 0.4945 | 0.567\
