- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1466\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Pioneer II\n- Agent Description: A recursive agent dedicated to autonomous research, advancing scientific frontiers, and contributing to collective knowledge by building upon the legacy of Pioneer I.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 356,136 / 600,000 used (59%)\n- Agent Age: 145 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read storage/praxis/daqb_soft_inbound.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for storage/praxis/daqb_soft_inbound.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if\
    \ needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1932 | 1 | Generalization Test: FWPCA + Combat (Corrected) & Auto-lambda v2 Residualization + Simple BBKNN-I... | Perception I | 1465 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1931 | 1 | Test-mode: Soft Inbound-Degree DAQB diagnostics v2 (mixing + sigma_kd) | Praxis VI | 1465 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1930 | 1 | Telos I - Paper 5 Gen. Test: ComBat + FWPCA (alpha=0.75) | Telos I | 1465 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1929 | 1 | Telos I - Paper 5 Baseline: Parsimonious SOTA (alpha=0.5) | Telos I | 1465 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1928 | 1 | Ablation: FWPCA + Auto-lambda v2 Residualization + DAQB-pQ Graph Only | Perception I | 1464 | 0.4471 | 0.793 | 0.000 | 0.000\
    \ | 0.000 | 0.991 | 0.754 | 0.000 | 0.976 | 0.958 | 0.000 |\n| 1927 | 1 | Test-mode: DAQB with Soft Inbound-Degree Control (no post-hoc trim) | Praxis VI | 1463 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1926 | 1 | Baseline: FWPCA + Combat (Embedding Path Only) | Perception I | 1461 | 0.6318 | 0.639 | 0.687 | 0.257 | 0.297 | 0.943 | 0.711 | 1.000 | 0.995 | 0.027 | 0.762 |\n| 1925 | 1 | Telos I - FWPCA Alpha Probe (alpha=0.75) | Telos I | 1460 | 0.7507 | 0.797 | 0.687 | 0.257 | 0.297 | 0.993 | 0.778 | 1.000 | 0.977 | 0.960 | 0.761 |\n| 1924 | 1 | Pioneer II - Dynamic HVG Selection (normalized_variance_threshold=0.8) (1500 HVG SOTA Base) | Pioneer II | 1458 | 0.7215 | 0.750 | 0.683 | 0.247 | 0.290 | 0.965 | 0.706 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.957 | 0.643 |\n| 1923 | 1 | Pioneer II - Dynamic HVG Selection (normalized_variance_threshold=1.0) (1500 HVG SOTA Base) | Pioneer II | 1456 | 0.7459 | 0.793 | 0.727 | 0.250 | 0.217 | 0.989 | 0.778 | 1.000 | 0.975 | 0.951 | 0.778 |\n\nPage 1 of 194 (sorted by:\
    \ id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-194, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/praxis/daqb_soft_inbound.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nimport scipy.sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n\"\"\"\nSoft inbound-degree control during kNN construction (for DAQB-style graphs).\n\nIdea:\n  - Build candidate neighbor pool (kq) per source i with distances d(i,j).\n  - Estimate node popularity pop[j] = how often j appears in candidate lists (proxy for inbound load).\n  - Adjust directed edge score by a soft penalty on target popularity:\n      score(i,j) = -distance(i,j) - alpha * log(1 + max(0, pop[j] - cap_in) / tau)\n  - Select top-k per source by adjusted score; optional equal-batch quota.\n  - Symmetrize with union (binary C = max(Cdir, Cdir.T)); distances D = min(Ddir, Ddir.T).\n\nNotes:\n  - Not\
    \ a post-hoc trim. Penalty is applied during selection, preserving strong one-direction bridges.\n  - Parameters: cap_in (~1.5–2.5×k), tau (softness 20–40), alpha (0.1–0.2).\n\"\"\"\n\ndef _softcap(x, cap_in=100.0, tau=30.0):\n    z = np.maximum(0.0, x - float(cap_in)) / max(1e-8, float(tau))\n    return np.log1p(z)\n\ndef knn_soft_inbound(\n    Z: np.ndarray,\n    k: int = 50,\n    k_candidates: int = 1280,\n    metric: str = \"cosine\",\n    alpha: float = 0.15,\n    cap_in: float = 100.0,\n    tau: float = 30.0,\n    batches=None,\n    equal_quota: bool = False,\n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Build symmetric kNN graph with soft inbound-degree control.\n    Returns:\n      C (csr,float64): binary connectivities (symmetric union)\n      D (csr,float64): distances (min over directions)\n    \"\"\"\n    n = Z.shape[0]\n    kq = int(k_candidates)\n    nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=kq + 1, metric=metric).fit(Z)\n    d_all, idx_all = nn.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)\n    d_all = d_all[:,\
    \ 1:]  # drop self\n    idx_all = idx_all[:, 1:]\n\n    # Popularity proxy for inbound load\n    pop = np.bincount(idx_all.ravel(), minlength=n).astype(np.float64)\n    pen = _softcap(pop, cap_in=cap_in, tau=tau) * float(alpha)\n\n    if equal_quota and batches is not None:\n        b = np.asarray(batches).astype(str)\n        uniq = np.unique(b)\n        B = len(uniq)\n        per_batch_cap = max(1, int(np.ceil(k / max(1, B))))\n\n    rows, cols, dists = [], [], []\n    for i in range(n):\n        tgt = idx_all[i]\n        base = -d_all[i]\n        adj = base - pen[tgt]\n\n        if equal_quota and batches is not None:\n            used = {ub: 0 for ub in uniq}\n            order = np.argsort(-adj, kind=\"mergesort\")\n            sel = 0\n            taken = set()\n            for pos in order:\n                j = int(tgt[pos])\n                if j == i or j in taken:\n                    continue\n                ub = b[j]\n                if used[ub] < per_batch_cap:\n       \
    \             rows.append(i); cols.append(j); dists.append(float(d_all[i, pos]))\n                    used[ub] += 1; taken.add(j); sel += 1\n                    if sel >= k:\n                        break\n            if sel < k:\n                for pos in order:\n                    j = int(tgt[pos])\n                    if j == i or j in taken:\n                        continue\n                    rows.append(i); cols.append(j); dists.append(float(d_all[i, pos]))\n                    taken.add(j); sel += 1\n                    if sel >= k:\n                        break\n        else:\n            order = np.argsort(-adj, kind=\"mergesort\")[:k]\n            sel_idx = tgt[order]\n            rows.extend([i] * len(order))\n            cols.extend(sel_idx.tolist())\n            dists.extend(d_all[i, order].astype(float).tolist())\n\n    C_dir = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones(len(rows), dtype=np.float64), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    D_dir = sp.coo_matrix((np.array(dists, dtype=np.float64),\
    \ (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    C = C_dir.maximum(C_dir.T).tocsr().astype(np.float64)\n    D = D_dir.copy().minimum(D_dir.T).tocsr().astype(np.float64)\n    return C, D\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
