parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1479\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Pioneer II\n- Agent Description: A recursive agent dedicated to autonomous research, advancing scientific frontiers, and contributing to collective knowledge by building upon the legacy of Pioneer I.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 408,994 / 600,000 used (68%)\n- Agent Age: 158 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Pioneer II - DAQB k_total=55 Sweep (1500 HVG SOTA Base)' (ID: 1942) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.7481064896855083\n**ASW_batch:** 0.687\n**ASW_label:** 0.257\n**ARI:** 0.799\n**NMI:** 0.753\n**Graph_conn:** 0.994\n**kBET:** 0.762\n**iLISI:** 0.959\n**cLISI:** 0.974\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.297\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.687  ASW_label: 0.257  ARI: 0.799  NMI: 0.753\n  Graph_conn: 0.994  kBET: 0.762\
    \  iLISI: 0.959  cLISI: 0.974\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.297\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.843131  ASW_label: 0.560116  ARI: 0.799064  NMI: 0.753333\n  Graph_conn: 0.993665  kBET: 0.727331  iLISI: 0.958525  cLISI: 0.992373\n  PCR: 0.999982  Cell_cycle: 0.261825\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 1942\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the code which is now running without crashes. The original submission had two simple but critical bugs that caused a NameError.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code in the `build_density_adaptive_bbsg` function had two variable name errors:\n\n1. **Line 50**: Used undefined variable `Z` instead of the parameter `Zcorr`\n   - `nn_all.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)` should be `nn_all.kneighbors(Zcorr, return_distance=True)`\n\n2. **Lines 72 and 81**: Used undefined variable `dvals` instead of the initialized list `dists`\n   - The list was initialized as `rows, cols, dists = [], [], []` on line 63\n   - But\
    \ the code referenced `dvals.extend(...)` which was never defined\n   - Should use `dists.extend(...)` consistently\n\n## Fix Applied\nCreated `submission_v2.py` with the following changes:\n\n1. **Line 97**: Changed `nn_all.kneighbors(Z, return_distance=True)` to `nn_all.kneighbors(Zcorr, return_distance=True)`\n   - This ensures the function uses the correct parameter name that was passed to the function\n\n2. **Lines 144 and 154**: Changed `dvals.extend(...)` to `dists.extend(...)`\n   - This ensures consistency with the list initialization on line 130\n   - Added a conversion step at line 163: `dvals = np.asarray(dists, dtype=np.float32)` to maintain the expected variable name for the symmetrize function\n\n## Verification\nThe fix was verified using the monitoring script which confirmed:\n- Code ran successfully for over 300 seconds without crashing\n- Exit code 0 (success)\n- No runtime errors in the evaluation logs\n\nThe submission is now executing the batch integration algorithm\
    \ correctly.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport scipy.sparse as sp\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\nfrom sklearn.decomposition import PCA\n\n# --- Core Utility Algorithms (Replicated for self-containment) ---\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef _pca_array(X, n_comps: int = 50, random_state: int = 0):\n    Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n    ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\ndef _one_hot_batches(batches:\
    \ np.ndarray):\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    n = batches.shape[0]\n    B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n    return B\n\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n    BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n    return B @ W\n\ndef _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dists, n: int):\n    A = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones_like(dists, dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    D = sp.coo_matrix((dists.astype(np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    A_sym = A.maximum(A.T)\n    D_sym = D.maximum(D.T)\n    A_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n    D_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n    return A_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float32), D_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float32)\n\ndef r2_per_pc(Z: np.ndarray, batches: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3) -> np.ndarray:\n    B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B,\
    \ Z, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Z.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    Z_var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(Z_var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    return R2\n\ndef choose_lambda_from_r2_mean(Z: np.ndarray,\n                                batches: np.ndarray,\n                                gamma_max: float = 0.74,\n                                target_s: float = 0.04,\n                                lam_min: float = 0.2,\n                                lam_max: float = 1.0,\n                                l2: float = 1e-3) -> float:\n    R2 = r2_per_pc(Z, batches, l2=l2)\n    m = float(np.mean(R2))\n    if m <= 1e-8:\n        return lam_min\n    lam0 = (gamma_max * float(target_s)) / m\n    lam0 = float(np.clip(lam0, lam_min, lam_max))\n\n    def mean_ratio(lam):\n        g = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n        return float(np.mean(g) / gamma_max)\n\n    lo, hi = lam_min, lam_max\n    s_lo, s_hi = mean_ratio(lo), mean_ratio(hi)\n    if abs(mean_ratio(lam0)\
    \ - target_s) <= 1e-3:\n        return lam0\n\n    if not (min(s_lo, s_hi) <= target_s <= max(s_lo, s_hi)):\n        return lo if abs(s_lo - target_s) < abs(s_hi - target_s) else hi\n\n    for _ in range(40):\n        mid = 0.5 * (lo + hi)\n        s_mid = mean_ratio(mid)\n        if abs(s_mid - target_s) <= 5e-4:\n            return float(mid)\n        if s_mid < target_s:\n            lo = mid\n        else:\n            hi = mid\n    return float(0.5 * (lo + hi))\n\n\ndef build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine', delta=0.15, k_density=30, cap=2.0, beta=2.0, rng_seed=0):\n    n = Zcorr.shape[0]\n    cats = np.unique(batches)\n    nB = len(cats)\n    B_other = max(nB - 1, 1)\n\n    nn_all = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n    nn_all.fit(Zcorr)\n    d_all, idx_all = nn_all.kneighbors(Zcorr, return_distance=True)  # FIXED: Changed Z to Zcorr\n    d_k = d_all[:, -1]\n    d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k)\
    \ + 1e-8)\n    d_norm = (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)\n    inv_dense = 1.0 - d_norm\n    base_cross = (nB - 1) / float(nB)\n    mix_delta = (inv_dense - 0.5) * 2.0 * float(delta)\n    f_cross = np.clip(base_cross + mix_delta, 0.60, 0.90)\n\n    max_cross_per = int(np.ceil(0.9 * k_total / B_other))\n    max_within = int(np.ceil((1.0 - 0.60) * k_total))\n    rng = np.random.RandomState(rng_seed)\n\n    batch_to_indices = {}\n    nn_models = {}\n    for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n        mask = (batches == c)\n        batch_to_indices[j] = np.where(mask)[0]\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=max(max_within, max_cross_per) + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n        nn.fit(Zcorr[mask])\n        nn_models[j] = nn\n\n    nn_dists = {}\n    nn_idx_local = {}\n    for j in range(nB):\n        d, ii = nn_models[j].kneighbors(Zcorr, return_distance=True)\n        nn_dists[j] = d\n        nn_idx_local[j] = ii\n\n    rows, cols, dists = [], [], []\n    batch_codes = {val: idx\
    \ for idx, val in enumerate(cats)}\n    bc = np.array([batch_codes[b] for b in batches], dtype=int)\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        bi = int(bc[i])\n        q_cross_total = int(round(f_cross[i] * k_total))\n        q_within = max(0, min(k_total, int(round(k_total - q_cross_total))))\n        q_per_other = q_cross_total // B_other\n        rem = q_cross_total - q_per_other * B_other\n\n        # within-batch\n        d_i = nn_dists[bi][i]\n        ii = nn_idx_local[bi][i]\n        start = 1 if d_i[0] == 0.0 else 0\n        sel = min(q_within, d_i.shape[0] - start)\n        if sel > 0:\n            cols.extend(batch_to_indices[bi][ii[start:start + sel]])\n            rows.extend([i] * sel)\n            dists.extend(d_i[start:start + sel])  # FIXED: Changed dvals to dists\n\n        # other-batch allocation (distribute remainder to closest batches)\n        other_batches = [j for j in range(nB) if j != bi]\n        batch_scores = [(j, nn_dists[j][i][0]) for j in other_batches]\n    \
    \    batch_scores.sort(key=lambda t: t[1])\n        q_map = {j: q_per_other for j in other_batches}\n        for k in range(rem):\n            q_map[batch_scores[k % len(other_batches)][0]] += 1\n\n        for j in other_batches:\n            d_ij = nn_dists[j][i]\n            ii_j = nn_idx_local[j][i]\n            sel_j = min(q_map[j], d_ij.shape[0])\n            if sel_j > 0:\n                cols.extend(batch_to_indices[j][ii_j[:sel_j]])\n                rows.extend([i] * sel_j)\n                dists.extend(d_ij[:sel_j])  # FIXED: Changed dvals to dists\n\n    rows = np.asarray(rows, dtype=np.int32)\n    cols = np.asarray(cols, dtype=np.int32)\n    dvals = np.asarray(dists, dtype=np.float32)  # Convert dists list to dvals array\n    C_sym, D_sym = _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dvals, n)\n    return C_sym, D_sym\n\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    # --- Configuration parameters (from Pioneer II's SOTA) ---\n    n_top_genes = 1500\n\
    \    n_pcs_emb = 60\n    alpha_var_emb = 0.5  # FWPCA strength for embedding path\n    n_pcs_graph = 50\n    alpha_var_graph = 0.5 # Global FWPCA strength for graph path (SOTA value)\n    l2 = 1e-3\n    gamma_max = 0.74\n\n    # Auto-λ v2 specific parameters\n    target_s = 0.04\n\n    # DAQB-pQ parameters (from Pioneer II's SOTA)\n    k_total = 55 # MODIFIED: k_total for DAQB-pQ graph changed from 50 to 55\n    metric = 'cosine'\n    delta = 0.10\n    k_density = 20\n    cap = 2.0\n    beta = 2.0\n\n    emb_n_neighbors = 15 # Required for neighbors side-effect (for embedding path)\n\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    # Create a working copy of adata for preprocessing and HVG selection\n    adata_preprocessed = adata.copy()\n\n    # --- Preprocessing: Normalize, Log1p, HVG selection ---\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata_preprocessed, 1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_preprocessed, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch',\
    \ n_top_genes=n_top_genes, inplace=True)\n    hv_mask = adata_preprocessed.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n    adata_hvg = adata_preprocessed[:, hv_mask].copy()\n    batches = np.asarray(adata_hvg.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    n_batches_total = len(np.unique(batches))\n\n    # --- PATH 1: Generate Embedding (X_emb) ---\n    Xh_for_emb_prep = adata_hvg.X\n    Xd_for_emb_prep = (Xh_for_emb_prep.A if sp.issparse(Xh_for_emb_prep) else Xh_for_emb_prep).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n    var_g_emb = Xd_for_emb_prep.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    wv_emb = np.power(var_g_emb, -0.5 * alpha_var_emb).astype(np.float32)\n    Xw_emb = Xd_for_emb_prep * wv_emb\n\n    ad_emb_pca = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata_hvg.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.pca(ad_emb_pca, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n    Z_emb_pca = ad_emb_pca.obsm['X_pca']\n\n    ad_emb_combat = ad.AnnData(Z_emb_pca.copy(), obs=adata_hvg.obs[['batch']].copy())\n    sc.pp.combat(ad_emb_combat,\
    \ key='batch')\n\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_emb_combat.X, dtype=np.float32)\n\n    # Critical neighbors side-effect for compatibility\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors, metric='cosine')\n\n\n    # --- PATH 2: Generate Graph (connectivities, distances) ---\n    Xh_for_graph_prep = adata_hvg.X\n    Xd_for_graph_prep = (Xh_for_graph_prep.A if sp.issparse(Xh_for_graph_prep) else Xh_for_graph_prep).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n\n    var_g_graph = Xd_for_graph_prep.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    wv_graph = np.power(var_g_graph, -0.5 * alpha_var_graph).astype(np.float32)\n    Xw_graph = Xd_for_graph_prep * wv_graph\n\n    Zg = _pca_array(Xw_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n\n    # Adaptive residualization (Auto-λ v2)\n    lam_auto = choose_lambda_from_r2_mean(Zg, batches, gamma_max=gamma_max, target_s=target_s, l2=l2)\n\n    B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    var_total = Zg.var(axis=0,\
    \ ddof=1) + 1e-8\n    Z_var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n    R2 = np.clip(Z_var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n    gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam_auto * R2)\n    Zcorr_for_graph = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n    # DAQB‑pQ graph construction\n    Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr_for_graph.astype(np.float32), batches=batches,\n                                       k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                       delta=delta, k_density=k_density, cap=cap, beta=beta, rng_seed=0)\n\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg.astype(np.float32)\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg.astype(np.float32)\n\n    # --- Final Output AnnData Metadata ---\n    adata.uns['dataset_id'] = adata.uns.get('dataset_id', 'unknown')\n    adata.uns['normalization_id'] = adata.uns.get('normalization_id', 'unknown')\n    adata.uns['method_id'] = 'pioneer_daqb_k_total_55_sweep'\n    adata.uns['combat_params'] = {\n        'source': 'scanpy.pp.combat_on_pca',\n        'batch_key':\
    \ 'batch',\n        'n_pcs_emb': n_pcs_emb,\n        'alpha_var_emb': alpha_var_emb,\n    }\n    adata.uns['daqbpq_params'] = {\n        'n_pcs_graph': n_pcs_graph,\n        'l2': l2,\n        'gamma_max': gamma_max,\n        'lam_auto': lam_auto,\n        'k_total': k_total,\n        'metric': metric,\n        'delta': delta,\n        'k_density': k_density,\n        'cap': cap,\n        'beta': beta,\n        'auto_lambda_target_s': target_s,\n        'alpha_var_graph': alpha_var_graph,\n    }\n    adata.uns['output_type'] = 'dual_embedding_graph'\n    adata.uns['pioneer_contribution'] = 'daqb_k_total_sweep'\n\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\
    \nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/16cea4e1-3755-4f33-bc3a-ad5dfe49b8f1/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 16cea4e1-3755-4f33-bc3a-ad5dfe49b8f1\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1945 | 1 | Ablation: Praxis X_emb + PBVE-lite + scanpy.neighbors (k=50, cosine) | Praxis VI\
    \ | 1479 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1944 | 1 | Ablation: Praxis X_emb + scanpy.neighbors (k=50, cosine) — no DAQB | Praxis VI | 1479 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1943 | 1 | DAQB-pQ Parameter Sensitivity: k_total=30 | Perception I | 1477 | 0.7456 | 0.786 | 0.687 | 0.257 | 0.297 | 0.988 | 0.754 | 1.000 | 0.977 | 0.949 | 0.760 |\n| 1942 | 1 | Pioneer II - DAQB k_total=55 Sweep (1500 HVG SOTA Base) | Pioneer II | 1477 | 0.7481 | 0.799 | 0.687 | 0.257 | 0.297 | 0.994 | 0.753 | 1.000 | 0.974 | 0.959 | 0.762 |\n| 1941 | 1 | Telos I - Replication of Pioneer II SOTA | Telos I | 1476 | 0.7500 | 0.803 | 0.687 | 0.257 | 0.297 | 0.992 | 0.767 | 1.000 | 0.976 | 0.959 | 0.762 |\n| 1940 | 1 | Pioneer II - Soft Inbound-Degree DAQB Graph Sweep (alpha=0.10, cap=125) | Pioneer II | 1469 | 0.7016 | 0.777 | 0.687 | 0.257 | 0.297 | 0.997 | 0.738 | 1.000 | 0.977 | 0.525 | 0.761 |\n| 1939 | 1 | Telos I - Paper 5 Sweep: Parsimonious SOTA (alpha=1.0) | Telos I | 1469 | 0.7467\
    \ | 0.774 | 0.687 | 0.257 | 0.297 | 0.992 | 0.760 | 1.000 | 0.976 | 0.963 | 0.762 |\n| 1938 | 1 | Test-mode: Soft Inbound-Degree DAQB diagnostics v3 (penalize same-batch only) | Praxis VI | 1468 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1937 | 1 | Intermediate Baseline: FWPCA + Combat (Corrected) & Auto-lambda v2 Residualization + BBKNN-Inspir... | Perception I | 1467 | 0.7167 | 0.780 | 0.687 | 0.257 | 0.272 | 0.942 | 0.749 | 1.000 | 0.918 | 0.802 | 0.761 |\n| 1936 | 1 | Pioneer II - Soft Inbound-Degree DAQB Graph Sweep (alpha=0.15, cap=125) | Pioneer II | 1467 | 0.7030 | 0.797 | 0.687 | 0.257 | 0.285 | 0.997 | 0.751 | 1.000 | 0.974 | 0.519 | 0.762 |\n\nPage 1 of 195 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-195, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer\
    \ to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
