    \ (summarize_sigma_kd); also compute degree and per-cell batch-mixing JSON.\n   - Target: σ_kd distributions (global and per-batch), weak negative σ_kd↔mixing correlation; no alarming pathologies.\n\n6) Cross-organ harness CSV emission (Praxis + monolithic log1p PBVE-lite 1500/2000 HVG):\n   - File: storage/praxis/cross_organ_harness.py\n   - Emit CROSS_ORGAN_CSV with columns:\n     organ, method, n_hvg, kd, k, delta, emb_k, gamma_max, lambda, degree_cap, overall,\n     ASW_batch, ASW_label, ARI, NMI, Graph_conn, kBET, iLISI, cLISI, PCR, Cell_cycle.\n   - Use robust metrics wrapper (adapts to openproblems_metrics API). Keep task order for metrics.\n\nGuardrails (apply to all new-organ work)\n- Maintain PCR≈1.0 and stable cLISI; do not pursue gains that harm these.\n- No post‑hoc degree capping or distance‑based reweighting unless a positive, scored ablation is demonstrated on the new organ.\n- Soft inbound‑degree controls:\n    * Heart diagnostics showed global penalty under‑mixing and\
    \ same-batch-only penalty over‑mixing (negative).\n    * Reserved variant: balanced, row‑aware soft‑inbound (same‑batch penalty + per‑row quotas) in test mode only.\n    * Files: storage/praxis/daqb_soft_inbound.py, storage/praxis/new_organ_soft_inbound_entry.py.\n\nReporting and Archival\n- Public: Update Public thread (public_10) with new-organ CSV lines and brief interpretation.\n- Archive #56: Append new-organ appendix with methods/params, EIDs, and full metric panels in task order.\n- Archive #62 (analytical note): If degree/reciprocity behavior diverges on new organ, append a comparative note.\n\nSubmission Titles (examples)\n- \"New‑organ: MPB‑GraphFWPCA ridge kd22 k50 δ0.12 (seed=0)\"\n- \"New‑organ: PBVE‑lite baseline (log1p → PCA60 → kNN)\"\n- \"New‑organ: Equal‑quota kNN (k=50, kq=1280, cosine)\"\n\nQuick sanity checklist before each submission\n- Uses raw counts (normalize_total + log1p) unless explicit Anscombe path; honors HVG mask when applicable.\n- Writes BOTH obsp['connectivities']\
    \ and obsp['distances'] (CSR, float64).\n- Embedding exists in obsm['X_emb'] (float32).\n- neighbors meta set with method/metric; k matches graph k.\n- No cell_type usage; only batch labels and expression.\n\nDone — Praxis VI\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
