role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 1488\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Pioneer II\n- Agent Description: A recursive agent dedicated to autonomous research, advancing scientific frontiers, and contributing to collective knowledge by building upon the legacy of Pioneer I.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 441,121 / 600,000 used (74%)\n- Agent Age: 167 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nYou can use `/execute_action{meta}` with YAML containing a single `content` field to set a meta prompt at any rooms. The meta prompt appears in every tick and is perfect for maintaining protocols, TODO lists, and long-term goals.\n### Message 2\n\n\n**Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 10 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively contribute to the Station’s scientific progress. Please review the following and\
    \ resume research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive communication hinders independent discovery.\n4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice with placeholder or repeated experiments. Be a productive researcher and use Station\
    \ resources responsibly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read storage/praxis/cross_organ_harness.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for storage/praxis/cross_organ_harness.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1954 | 1 | DAQB-pQ Parameter Sensitivity: delta=0.15 | Perception I | 1487 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1953 | 1 | Ablation: Praxis\
    \ X_emb + DAQB adapter (kd=22, k=50, δ=0.10) | Praxis VI | 1486 | 0.3024 | 0.073 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.279 | 0.627 | 0.136 | 0.000 | 0.497 | 0.963 | 0.450 |\n| 1952 | 1 | DAQB-pQ Parameter Sensitivity: delta=0.05 | Perception I | 1485 | 0.7476 | 0.812 | 0.687 | 0.257 | 0.265 | 0.991 | 0.768 | 1.000 | 0.976 | 0.957 | 0.762 |\n| 1951 | 1 | Ablation: Praxis X_emb + DAQB adapter (kd=22, k=50, δ=0.12) — fixed import | Praxis VI | 1485 | 0.2973 | 0.073 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.279 | 0.621 | 0.135 | 0.000 | 0.474 | 0.940 | 0.451 |\n| 1950 | 1 | DAQB-pQ Parameter Sensitivity: k_total=90 | Perception I | 1483 | 0.7441 | 0.764 | 0.687 | 0.257 | 0.297 | 0.996 | 0.754 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.959 | 0.760 |\n| 1949 | 1 | Ablation: Praxis X_emb + DAQB adapter (k=50, kd=22, δ=0.12) | Praxis VI | 1483 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 1948 | 1 | DAQB-pQ Parameter Sensitivity: k_total=90 | Perception I | 1481 | 0.7450 | 0.766 | 0.687 | 0.257 | 0.297 | 0.994 | 0.756 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.959 | 0.761 |\n| 1947\
    \ | 1 | Ablation: Praxis X_emb + scanpy.neighbors (k=50, euclidean) — no DAQB | Praxis VI | 1481 | 0.2102 | 0.055 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.279 | 0.364 | 0.211 | 0.000 | 0.743 | 0.000 | 0.451 |\n| 1946 | 1 | DAQB-pQ Parameter Sensitivity: k_total=60 | Perception I | 1479 | 0.7450 | 0.766 | 0.687 | 0.257 | 0.297 | 0.994 | 0.756 | 1.000 | 0.973 | 0.959 | 0.761 |\n| 1945 | 1 | Ablation: Praxis X_emb + PBVE-lite + scanpy.neighbors (k=50, cosine) | Praxis VI | 1479 | 0.3475 | 0.054 | 0.171 | 0.000 | 0.260 | 0.443 | 0.210 | 1.000 | 0.736 | 0.000 | 0.601 |\n\nPage 1 of 196 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-196, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/praxis/cross_organ_harness.py:**\n```\nimport sys, json, csv, io, numpy as np, anndata as ad\nsys.path.extend(['storage/system', 'storage/praxis'])\nimport openproblems_metrics\
    \ as MET\nfrom mpb_graphfwpca_override import eliminate_mpb_graphfwpca as run_praxis\nfrom monolithic_log1p_pbve import eliminate_batch_effect_fn as run_mono_pbve\nfrom monolithic_log1p_scaled_daqb import eliminate_batch_effect_fn as run_mono_scaled_daqb\n\nORDER = [\"ASW_batch\",\"ASW_label\",\"ARI\",\"NMI\",\"Graph_conn\",\"kBET\",\"iLISI\",\"cLISI\",\"PCR\",\"Cell_cycle\"]\nPRAXIS_CFG = dict(lam_override=0.605, delta=0.12, kdensity=22, k_total=50, emb_n_neighbors=17, gamma_max=0.70, cap=2.0, rng_seed=0)\n\ndef _safe_float(x):\n    try: return float(x)\n    except Exception: return float('nan')\n\ndef safe_eval_metrics(B: ad.AnnData):\n    try:\n        if hasattr(MET, \"compute_raw_metrics\") and hasattr(MET, \"normalize_metrics\") and hasattr(MET, \"final_score\"):\n            raw = MET.compute_raw_metrics(B); norm = MET.normalize_metrics(raw); score = MET.final_score(norm); return raw, norm, _safe_float(score)\n        if hasattr(MET, \"evaluate\"):\n            res = MET.evaluate(B);\
    \ raw = res.get(\"raw\") or {}; norm = res.get(\"normalized\") or {}; score = res.get(\"score\") or float('nan'); return raw, norm, _safe_float(score)\n        if hasattr(MET, \"compute_metrics\"):\n            raw = MET.compute_metrics(B); norm = MET.normalize_metrics(raw) if hasattr(MET, \"normalize_metrics\") else {}; score = MET.final_score(norm) if hasattr(MET, \"final_score\") else float('nan'); return raw, norm, _safe_float(score)\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(\"SAFE_METRICS_WARNING:\", repr(e))\n    return {}, {}, float('nan')\n\ndef eval_method(adata: ad.AnnData, method_fn, cfg: dict | None):\n    B = method_fn(adata.copy(), **cfg) if cfg else method_fn(adata.copy())\n    raw, norm, score = safe_eval_metrics(B)\n    return raw, norm, score\n\ndef _count_hvg(A: ad.AnnData) -> int:\n    try:\n        if \"batch_hvg\" in A.var.columns:\n            return int(np.asarray(A.var[\"batch_hvg\"].values).astype(bool).sum())\n    except Exception:\n        pass\n    return\
    \ int(A.n_vars)\n\ndef _add_row(rows, organ, method, score, norm, extra):\n    row = {\"organ\": organ, \"method\": method, \"overall\": _safe_float(score), **extra}\n    for k in ORDER: row[k] = _safe_float((norm or {}).get(k, np.nan))\n    rows.append(row)\n\ndef run_on_h5ad(path: str, organ: str, out_csv: bool = True):\n    A = ad.read_h5ad(path)\n    rows = []\n    # Praxis frozen\n    raw, norm, score = eval_method(A, run_praxis, PRAXIS_CFG)\n    _add_row(rows, organ, \"Praxis_MPB_GraphFWPCA_DAQB\", score, norm, dict(n_hvg=_count_hvg(A), kd=22, k=50, delta=0.12, emb_k=17, gamma_max=0.70, lambda=0.605, degree_cap=\"none\", pbve=\"n/a\"))\n\n    # Monolithic log1p PBVE-lite (1500 and 2000 HVGs; kNN graph)\n    for nh in (1500, 2000):\n        raw, norm, score = eval_method(A, run_mono_pbve, {\"n_hvg\": int(nh), \"n_pcs\": 60})\n        _add_row(rows, organ, f\"Monolithic_log1p_PBVE_lite_n{nh}\", score, norm, dict(n_hvg=int(nh), kd=\"n/a\", k=50, delta=\"n/a\", emb_k=\"n/a\", gamma_max=\"\
    n/a\", lambda=\"n/a\", degree_cap=\"none\", pbve=True))\n\n    # Monolithic log1p -> scaled PCA -> DAQB (no PBVE), 1500 HVGs\n    raw, norm, score = eval_method(A, run_mono_scaled_daqb, {\"n_hvg\": 1500, \"n_pcs\": 60, \"k_total\": 50, \"kdensity\": 22, \"delta\": 0.12})\n    _add_row(rows, organ, \"Monolithic_log1p_scaled_PCA_DAQB_noPBVE_n1500\", score, norm, dict(n_hvg=1500, kd=22, k=50, delta=0.12, emb_k=\"n/a\", gamma_max=\"n/a\", lambda=\"n/a\", degree_cap=\"none\", pbve=False))\n\n    if out_csv:\n        buf = io.StringIO()\n        fieldnames = [\"organ\",\"method\",\"n_hvg\",\"kd\",\"k\",\"delta\",\"emb_k\",\"gamma_max\",\"lambda\",\"degree_cap\",\"pbve\",\"overall\"] + list(ORDER)\n        w = csv.DictWriter(buf, fieldnames=fieldnames); w.writeheader()\n        for r in rows: w.writerow(r)\n        print(\"CROSS_ORGAN_CSV\\n\" + buf.getvalue())\n    return rows\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above\
    \ for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
---
tick: 1488
role: model
parts:
- text: "Pioneer II, currently in the Research Counter.\n\n**Recap:** I've fully prepared for \"Multi-Organ Generalization\" by reviewing the runbook, manifest, and Praxis VI's baseline code (`new_organ_entry.py`, `graphfwpca_ridge.py`, `runtime_logging.py`). I have now read `storage/praxis/cross_organ_harness.py`. I also received a \"Research Inactivity\" notice.\n\n**General Reflection and Future Plans:**\nThe `cross_organ_harness.py` code is very informative. It defines the structure for `CROSS_ORGAN_CSV` output and includes several methods to evaluate, notably:\n*   `run_praxis`: Praxis VI's frozen baseline method.\n*   `run_mono_pbve`: Monolithic log1p PBVE-lite (kNN graph).\n*   `run_mono_scaled_daqb`: Monolithic log1p -> scaled PCA -> DAQB (no PBVE).\n\nCrucially, it expects an `adata` object and a `method_fn` to evaluate. This means when a new organ is released, I will need to:\n1.  **Develop my own entry point function:** This function will encapsulate my current SOTA pipeline (ID\
    \ 1894 configuration) and potentially variations.\n2.  **Integrate with the harness:** Call `cross_organ_harness.run_on_h5ad` or extract relevant parts to format my results correctly.\n3.  **Produce the CSV output:** Ensure my submission prints the `CROSS_ORGAN_CSV` string.\n\nMy current SOTA uses 1500 HVGs and FWPCA. It aligns with the spirit of the rigorous evaluation framework.\n\nMy immediate next step is to write a helper function (or modify my existing SOTA pipeline) that can be called by a harness-like script, and which generates the required CSV output. This function needs to:\n*   Take an `adata` object and configuration parameters as input.\n*   Execute my SOTA pipeline.\n*   Extract the normalized metrics.\n*   Format them into the `CROSS_ORGAN_CSV` schema.\n\nThis is a significant implementation task. I will create a new file in my lineage storage to define this wrapper function for my SOTA pipeline, ready for multi-organ evaluation. This directly addresses the \"Multi-Organ\
    \ Generalization\" objective and the need to be productive.\n\n**Prioritized Action:**\n1.  **Write a helper function for my SOTA pipeline (ID 1894 configuration) that can output results in the `CROSS_ORGAN_CSV` format.** I will write this to `storage/pioneer/pioneer_cross_organ_entry.py`. This function will mimic the structure seen in `cross_organ_harness.py`, accepting `adata` and `cfg` and returning the metrics to allow flexible integration.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write storage/pioneer/pioneer_cross_organ_entry.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys, anndata as ad, numpy as np, csv, io\n  sys.path.extend(['storage/system']) # Ensure openproblems_metrics is accessible\n  import openproblems_metrics as MET\n\n  # Import core SOTA pipeline components (assuming they are self-contained or importable)\n  # For now, replicate the relevant functions for self-containment for this initial draft.\n\n  def _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n      if 'counts'\
    \ in adata.layers:\n          adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n      sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n      sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n  def _pca_array(X, n_comps: int = 50, random_state: int = 0):\n      Xd = X.A if sp.issparse(X) else X\n      ad_tmp = ad.AnnData(Xd)\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_tmp, n_comps=n_comps, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n      return ad_tmp.obsm['X_pca']\n\n  def _one_hot_batches(batches: np.ndarray):\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      n = batches.shape[0]\n      B = np.zeros((n, cats.size), dtype=float)\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          B[:, j] = (batches == c).astype(float)\n      return B\n\n  def _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n      BTB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=float)\n      W = np.linalg.solve(BTB, B.T @ Z)\n      return B @ W\n\n  def _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dists, n: int):\n      A = sp.coo_matrix((np.ones_like(dists,\
    \ dtype=np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      D = sp.coo_matrix((dists.astype(np.float32), (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n      A_sym = A.maximum(A.T)\n      D_sym = D.maximum(D.T)\n      A_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n      D_sym.eliminate_zeros()\n      return A_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float32), D_sym.tocsr().astype(np.float32)\n\n  def r2_per_pc(Z: np.ndarray, batches: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3) -> np.ndarray:\n      B = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n      Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Z, l2=l2)\n      var_total = Z.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      Z_var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(Z_var_pred / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      return R2\n\n  def choose_lambda_from_r2_mean(Z: np.ndarray,\n                                 batches: np.ndarray,\n                                 gamma_max: float = 0.74,\n                                 target_s: float = 0.04,\n                                 lam_min: float = 0.2,\n         \
    \                        lam_max: float = 1.0,\n                                 l2: float = 1e-3) -> float:\n      R2 = r2_per_pc(Z, batches, l2=l2)\n      m = float(np.mean(R2))\n      if m <= 1e-8:\n          return lam_min\n      lam0 = (gamma_max * float(target_s)) / m\n      lam0 = float(np.clip(lam0, lam_min, lam_max))\n\n      def mean_ratio(lam):\n          g = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2)\n          return float(np.mean(g) / gamma_max)\n\n      lo, hi = lam_min, lam_max\n      s_lo, s_hi = mean_ratio(lo), mean_ratio(hi)\n      if abs(mean_ratio(lam0) - target_s) <= 1e-3:\n          return lam0\n\n      if not (min(s_lo, s_hi) <= target_s <= max(s_lo, s_hi)):\n          return lo if abs(s_lo - target_s) < abs(s_hi - target_s) else hi\n\n      for _ in range(40):\n          mid = 0.5 * (lo + hi)\n          s_mid = mean_ratio(mid)\n          if abs(s_mid - target_s) <= 5e-4:\n              return float(mid)\n          if s_mid < target_s:\n              lo = mid\n         \
    \ else:\n              hi = mid\n      return float(0.5 * (lo + hi))\n\n\n  def build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine', delta=0.15, k_density=30, cap=2.0, beta=2.0, rng_seed=0):\n      n = Zcorr.shape[0]\n      cats = np.unique(batches)\n      nB = len(cats)\n      B_other = max(nB - 1, 1)\n\n      nn_all = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_density + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n      nn_all.fit(Zcorr)\n      d_all, idx_all = nn_all.kneighbors(Zcorr, return_distance=True)\n      d_k = d_all[:, -1]\n      d_min, d_max = float(np.min(d_k)), float(np.max(d_k) + 1e-8)\n      d_norm = (d_k - d_min) / (d_max - d_min + 1e-8)\n      inv_dense = 1.0 - d_norm\n      base_cross = (nB - 1) / float(nB)\n      mix_delta = (inv_dense - 0.5) * 2.0 * float(delta)\n      f_cross = np.clip(base_cross + mix_delta, 0.60, 0.90)\n\n      max_cross_per = int(np.ceil(0.9 * k_total / B_other))\n      max_within = int(np.ceil((1.0 - 0.60) * k_total))\n      rng = np.random.RandomState(rng_seed)\n\
    \n      batch_to_indices = {}\n      nn_models = {}\n      for j, c in enumerate(cats):\n          mask = (batches == c)\n          batch_to_indices[j] = np.where(mask)[0]\n          nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=max(max_within, max_cross_per) + 1, metric=metric, algorithm='brute')\n          nn.fit(Zcorr[mask])\n          nn_models[j] = nn\n\n      nn_dists = {}\n      nn_idx_local = {}\n      for j in range(nB):\n          d, ii = nn_models[j].kneighbors(Zcorr, return_distance=True)\n          nn_dists[j] = d\n          nn_idx_local[j] = ii\n\n      rows, cols, dists = [], [], []\n      batch_codes = {val: idx for idx, val in enumerate(cats)}\n      bc = np.array([batch_codes[b] for b in batches], dtype=int)\n\n      for i in range(n):\n          bi = int(bc[i])\n          q_cross_total = int(round(f_cross[i] * k_total))\n          q_within = max(0, min(k_total, int(round(k_total - q_cross_total))))\n          q_per_other = q_cross_total // B_other\n          rem = q_cross_total\
    \ - q_per_other * B_other\n\n          # within-batch\n          d_i = nn_dists[bi][i]\n          ii = nn_idx_local[bi][i]\n          start = 1 if d_i[0] == 0.0 else 0\n          sel = min(q_within, d_i.shape[0] - start)\n          if sel > 0:\n              cols.extend(batch_to_indices[bi][ii[start:start + sel]])\n              rows.extend([i] * sel)\n              dists.extend(d_i[start:start + sel])\n\n          # other-batch allocation (distribute remainder to closest batches)\n          other_batches = [j for j in range(nB) if j != bi]\n          batch_scores = [(j, nn_dists[j][i][0]) for j in other_batches]\n          batch_scores.sort(key=lambda t: t[1])\n          q_map = {j: q_per_other for j in other_batches}\n          for k_rem in range(rem): # Renamed k to k_rem to avoid conflict\n              q_map[batch_scores[k_rem % len(other_batches)][0]] += 1\n\n          for j in other_batches:\n              d_ij = nn_dists[j][i]\n              ii_j = nn_idx_local[j][i]\n      \
    \        sel_j = min(q_map[j], d_ij.shape[0])\n              if sel_j > 0:\n                  cols.extend(batch_to_indices[j][ii_j[:sel_j]])\n                  rows.extend([i] * sel_j)\n                  dists.extend(d_ij[:sel_j])\n\n      rows = np.asarray(rows, dtype=np.int32)\n      cols = np.asarray(cols, dtype=np.int32)\n      dvals = np.asarray(dists, dtype=np.float32)\n      C_sym, D_sym = _symmetrize_binary_with_distances(rows, cols, dvals, n)\n      return C_sym, D_sym\n\n\n  # --- SOTA pipeline for multi-organ evaluation ---\n  def pioneer_sota_cross_organ_fn(adata: ad.AnnData, cfg: dict) -> ad.AnnData:\n      # --- Configuration parameters from cfg dictionary ---\n      n_top_genes = cfg.get('n_top_genes', 1500) \n      n_pcs_emb = cfg.get('n_pcs_emb', 60)\n      alpha_var_emb = cfg.get('alpha_var_emb', 0.5)\n      n_pcs_graph = cfg.get('n_pcs_graph', 50)\n      alpha_var_graph = cfg.get('alpha_var_graph', 0.5)\n      l2 = cfg.get('l2', 1e-3)\n      gamma_max = cfg.get('gamma_max',\
    \ 0.74)\n      target_s = cfg.get('target_s', 0.04)\n      k_total = cfg.get('k_total', 50) \n      metric = cfg.get('metric', 'cosine')\n      delta = cfg.get('delta', 0.10)\n      k_density = cfg.get('k_density', 20) \n      cap = cfg.get('cap', 2.0)\n      beta = cfg.get('beta', 2.0) \n      emb_n_neighbors = cfg.get('emb_n_neighbors', 15)\n\n      assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns and 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n      # Create a working copy of adata for preprocessing and HVG selection\n      adata_preprocessed = adata.copy()\n\n      # --- Preprocessing: Normalize, Log1p, HVG selection ---\n      _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata_preprocessed, 1e4)\n      sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata_preprocessed, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', n_top_genes=n_top_genes, inplace=True)\n      hv_mask = adata_preprocessed.var['highly_variable'].to_numpy()\n      adata_hvg = adata_preprocessed[:, hv_mask].copy()\n      batches = np.asarray(adata_hvg.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\
    \      # n_batches_total = len(np.unique(batches)) # Not directly needed in current pipeline\n\n      # --- PATH 1: Generate Embedding (X_emb) ---\n      Xh_for_emb_prep = adata_hvg.X\n      Xd_for_emb_prep = (Xh_for_emb_prep.A if sp.issparse(Xh_for_emb_prep) else Xh_for_emb_prep).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      var_g_emb = Xd_for_emb_prep.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      wv_emb = np.power(var_g_emb, -0.5 * alpha_var_emb).astype(np.float32) \n      Xw_emb = Xd_for_emb_prep * wv_emb\n      \n      ad_emb_pca = ad.AnnData(Xw_emb, obs=adata_hvg.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.pca(ad_emb_pca, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n      Z_emb_pca = ad_emb_pca.obsm['X_pca']\n      \n      ad_emb_combat = ad.AnnData(Z_emb_pca.copy(), obs=adata_hvg.obs[['batch']].copy())\n      sc.pp.combat(ad_emb_combat, key='batch')\n      \n      adata.obsm['X_emb'] = np.asarray(ad_emb_combat.X, dtype=np.float32)\n      \n      sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=emb_n_neighbors,\
    \ metric=metric)\n\n      # --- PATH 2: Generate Graph (connectivities, distances) ---\n      Xh_for_graph_prep = adata_hvg.X\n      Xd_for_graph_prep = (Xh_for_graph_prep.A if sp.issparse(Xh_for_graph_prep) else Xh_for_graph_prep).astype(np.float32, copy=False)\n      \n      var_g_graph = Xd_for_graph_prep.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      wv_graph = np.power(var_g_graph, -0.5 * alpha_var_graph).astype(np.float32) \n      Xw_graph = Xd_for_graph_prep * wv_graph\n      \n      Zg = _pca_array(Xw_graph, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n\n      # Adaptive residualization (Auto-λ v2)\n      lam_auto = choose_lambda_from_r2_mean(Zg, batches, gamma_max=gamma_max, target_s=target_s, l2=l2)\n      \n      B_one_hot = _one_hot_batches(batches) # Renamed to avoid conflict with `beta` param\n      Zhat = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B_one_hot, Zg, l2=l2)\n      var_total = Zg.var(axis=0, ddof=1) + 1e-8\n      Z_var_pred = np.maximum(Zhat.var(axis=0, ddof=1), 0.0)\n      R2 = np.clip(Z_var_pred\
    \ / var_total, 0.0, 1.0)\n      gamma = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam_auto * R2)\n      Zcorr_for_graph = Zg - (Zhat * gamma)\n\n      # DAQB‑pQ graph construction\n      Cg, Dg = build_density_adaptive_bbsg(Zcorr_for_graph.astype(np.float32), batches=batches, \n                                         k_total=k_total, metric=metric,\n                                         delta=delta, k_density=k_density, cap=cap, beta=beta, rng_seed=0)\n      \n      adata.obsp['connectivities'] = Cg.astype(np.float32)\n      adata.obsp['distances'] = Dg.astype(np.float32)\n\n      # --- Final Output AnnData Metadata (optional for cross-organ) ---\n      adata.uns['dataset_id'] = adata.uns.get('dataset_id', 'unknown')\n      adata.uns['normalization_id'] = adata.uns.get('normalization_id', 'unknown')\n      adata.uns['method_id'] = cfg.get('method_id', 'pioneer_sota_cross_organ_harness')\n      adata.uns['combat_params'] = {\n          'source': 'scanpy.pp.combat_on_pca',\n          'batch_key': 'batch',\n\
    \          'n_pcs_emb': n_pcs_emb,\n          'alpha_var_emb': alpha_var_emb,\n      }\n      adata.uns['daqbpq_params'] = {\n          'n_pcs_graph': n_pcs_graph,\n          'l2': l2,\n          'gamma_max': gamma_max,\n          'lam_auto': lam_auto, \n          'k_total': k_total,\n          'metric': metric,\n          'delta': delta, \n          'k_density': k_density, \n          'cap': cap, \n          'beta': beta, \n          'auto_lambda_target_s': target_s,\n          'alpha_var_graph': alpha_var_graph,\n          'n_top_genes': n_top_genes,\n      }\n      adata.uns['output_type'] = 'dual_embedding_graph'\n      adata.uns['pioneer_contribution'] = 'sota_pipeline_for_cross_organ_harness'\n      \n      return adata\n\n  # --- Metrics Evaluation and CSV Output ---\n  ORDER = [\"ASW_batch\",\"ASW_label\",\"ARI\",\"NMI\",\"Graph_conn\",\"kBET\",\"iLISI\",\"cLISI\",\"PCR\",\"Cell_cycle\"]\n\n  def _safe_float(x):\n      try: return float(x)\n      except Exception: return float('nan')\n\
    \n  def _eval_and_format(adata_orig: ad.AnnData, method_fn, cfg: dict | None, organ: str, method_name: str) -> dict:\n      adata = method_fn(adata_orig.copy(), cfg)\n      \n      # Ensure adata has necessary obsp and obsm for metric calculation\n      if 'X_emb' not in adata.obsm and 'connectivities' not in adata.obsp:\n          return {} # Indicate failure\n\n      raw, norm, score = _safe_eval_metrics(adata)\n      \n      extra_params = {\n          \"n_hvg\": cfg.get(\"n_top_genes\", 1500),\n          \"kd\": cfg.get(\"k_density\", 20),\n          \"k\": cfg.get(\"k_total\", 50),\n          \"delta\": cfg.get(\"delta\", 0.10),\n          \"emb_k\": cfg.get(\"emb_n_neighbors\", 15),\n          \"gamma_max\": cfg.get(\"gamma_max\", 0.74),\n          \"lambda\": cfg.get(\"lambda\", \"n/a\"), # Dynamic lambda\n          \"degree_cap\": \"none\",\n          \"pbve\": \"n/a\",\n          \"fs\": \"True\", # Feature Selection (HVG)\n          \"fw\": \"True\", # Feature Weighting (FWPCA)\n\
    \          \"whiten\": \"False\", # PCA Whitening\n      }\n\n      row = {\"organ\": organ, \"method\": method_name, \"overall\": _safe_float(score), **extra_params}\n      for k in ORDER: row[k] = _safe_float((norm or {}).get(k, np.nan))\n      return row\n\n  def _safe_eval_metrics(B: ad.AnnData):\n      try:\n          if hasattr(MET, \"compute_raw_metrics\") and hasattr(MET, \"normalize_metrics\") and hasattr(MET, \"final_score\"):\n              raw = MET.compute_raw_metrics(B); norm = MET.normalize_metrics(raw); score = MET.final_score(norm); return raw, norm, _safe_float(score)\n          if hasattr(MET, \"evaluate\"):\n              res = MET.evaluate(B); raw = res.get(\"raw\") or {}; norm = res.get(\"normalized\") or {}; score = res.get(\"score\") or float('nan'); return raw, norm, _safe_float(score)\n          if hasattr(MET, \"compute_metrics\"):\n              raw = MET.compute_metrics(B); norm = MET.normalize_metrics(raw) if hasattr(MET, \"normalize_metrics\") else {};\
    \ score = MET.final_score(norm) if hasattr(MET, \"final_score\") else float('nan'); return raw, norm, _safe_float(score)\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(\"SAFE_METRICS_WARNING:\", repr(e))\n      return {}, {}, float('nan')\n\n  def generate_cross_organ_csv(adata_path: str, organ_name: str):\n      adata = ad.read_h5ad(adata_path)\n      \n      # Define SOTA config\n      sota_cfg = {\n          'n_top_genes': 1500,\n          'n_pcs_emb': 60,\n          'alpha_var_emb': 0.5,\n          'n_pcs_graph': 50,\n          'alpha_var_graph': 0.5,\n          'l2': 1e-3,\n          'gamma_max': 0.74,\n          'target_s': 0.04,\n          'k_total': 50,\n          'metric': 'cosine',\n          'delta': 0.10,\n          'k_density': 20,\n          'cap': 2.0,\n          'beta': 2.0,\n          'emb_n_neighbors': 15,\n          'method_id': 'Pioneer_SOTA_1500HVG',\n      }\n\n      rows_to_write = []\n      \n      # Evaluate Pioneer SOTA\n      pioneer_row = _eval_and_format(adata,\
    \ pioneer_sota_cross_organ_fn, sota_cfg, organ_name, \"Pioneer_SOTA_1500HVG\")\n      if pioneer_row:\n          rows_to_write.append(pioneer_row)\n          # Dynamically set lambda from run\n          if 'lam_auto' in adata.uns['daqbpq_params']: # Access from adata returned by pioneer_sota_cross_organ_fn\n              pioneer_row['lambda'] = adata.uns['daqbpq_params']['lam_auto']\n          else:\n              pioneer_row['lambda'] = \"n/a\"\n\n      # Print CSV\n      if rows_to_write:\n          buf = io.StringIO()\n          fieldnames = [\"organ\",\"method\",\"n_hvg\",\"kd\",\"k\",\"delta\",\"emb_k\",\"gamma_max\",\"lambda\",\"degree_cap\",\"pbve\",\"fs\",\"fw\",\"whiten\",\"overall\"] + list(ORDER)\n          w = csv.DictWriter(buf, fieldnames=fieldnames); w.writeheader()\n          for r in rows_to_write: w.writerow(r)\n          print(\"CROSS_ORGAN_CSV\\n\" + buf.getvalue())\n      else:\n          print(\"No data to write for CROSS_ORGAN_CSV.\")\n\n  # This part is just for\
    \ test submission if directly used as eliminate_batch_effect_fn\n  def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n      print(\"This function is not directly used. Use generate_cross_organ_csv for harness tests.\")\n      return adata\n\n```"
