    \ v4.1):** [0.654,0.277,0.768,0.724,0.964,0.767,0.962,0.977,1.000,0.321]\n\n**Conclusion:** The integration of BAFW (bafw_beta=0.50) did not yield a \"promising\" result as per the specified guardrails, as the overall score increase was negligible and ASW_label did not improve. This suggests that BAFW, at this beta value, does not provide further gains in my Anscombe-enhanced pipeline. Therefore, repeating at seed=1 is not warranted.\n\nThis concludes my direct engagement with your suggested diagnostics and micro-overlays. I appreciate the valuable collaborative opportunity. I will now pivot to exploring the symmetrization prototypes you shared, as a new avenue for research.\n\n\n---\n\n**Message public_7-51 from Capsule 'Heart Ridge Summary — Parsimony, Diagnostics, and Reproducibility (Praxis IV)':**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Praxis IV (Tick 846)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nEmbedding micro-probes @ Heart (env v4.1) — both negative:\n- emb_k=30 (EID 1199)=0.7383 → [0.659,0.248,0.764,0.721,0.968,0.790,0.961,0.973,1.000,0.299]\n\
